# DOES THE PUBLISHED DISK START? Boot it, look, and kill it - nothing else.
#
# THE CLAIM THE INSTALL LEG CANNOT MAKE. NetBSD's install walk ends with the sets extracted and the
# configuration menu answered; this is the file that says the firmware starts the disk and the system
# comes up.
#
# BIOS, NOT UEFI, BECAUSE THE INSTALL LEG WRITES MBR + BIOS BOOTBLOCKS. MEASURED on the disk the UEFI
# path published:
#
#	BdsDxe: failed to load Boot0002 "UEFI Misc Device" from PciRoot(0x0)/Pci(0x5,0x0): Not Found
#	BdsDxe: No bootable option or device was found.
#
# A walk names its own qemu arguments, so this leg boots the same way the install leg installed: q35
# with no OVMF at all, and the disk as bootindex=0.
#
# AND THE LOADER'S OWN WORDS ARE THE GATE, NOT OCR. MEASURED on a disk that does boot its loader:
#
#	booting hd0a:netbsd.old - starting in 0 seconds.
#	open netbsd.old: No such file or directory
#	booting hd0a:netbsd/kernel - starting in 0 seconds.
#
# `booting hd0a:` is bootxx having found and started the ffs, which no unbootable disk can print. The
# console is a serial file the engine already writes, so `until ... from console` reads it directly.
#
# IT PUBLISHES NO DISK: `out:` is empty in the stage that runs this. The artifact is the recording.
walkthrough "the published disk starts - nothing else"
resolution 1920x1080
recording_resolution 1920x1080

step "boot the published disk"
  boot
    machine "q35,accel=kvm,vmport=off"
    args [["-cpu", "Skylake-Client-v4"], ["-smp", "4"], ["-m", "2048"], ["-chardev", "socket,id=qga0,path=qga.sock,server=on,wait=off"], ["-device", "virtio-serial"], ["-device", "virtserialport,chardev=qga0,name=org.qemu.guest_agent.0"], ["-device", "VGA,xres=1920,yres=1080,vgamem_mb=32"], ["-device", "qemu-xhci,id=xhci"], ["-device", "usb-tablet,bus=xhci.0"], ["-device", "usb-kbd,bus=xhci.0"], ["-drive", "file=disk.qcow2,if=none,format=qcow2,discard=unmap,id=target"], ["-device", "virtio-blk-pci,drive=target,bootindex=0"], ["-audiodev", "none,id=snd0"], ["-device", "ich9-intel-hda"], ["-device", "hda-duplex,audiodev=snd0"], ["-netdev", "tap,id=net0,ifname=qemutap0,script=no,downscript=no"], ["-device", "virtio-net-pci,netdev=net0,mac=52:54:00:56:4d:01,romfile=,host_mtu=1450"]]
    timeout 600

# THE LOADER'S OWN LINE. `booting hd0a:` is bootxx having read the disklabel and started the file
# system; a disk without bootblocks prints nothing at all here.
step "the boot loader started the installed file system"
  until "booting hd"
  from console
  timeout 300

# THREE MINUTES OF RECORDING, AND NOTHING IS READ FROM IT. Every guest draws a different boot
# sequence, so a brightness or content threshold here would either be tuned to one of them or be so
# loose it could not fail. What this walk claims is checked above, on the console.
step "record three minutes of the boot"
  settle 180

step "stop the machine"
  stop kill
  timeout 120
